📗
  /todos: the Nest-style controller.

    GET    /todos           list (optional ?done=true|false)
    GET    /todos/:id:int   one todo or 404
    POST   /todos           {"title": "..."} → 201
    PUT    /todos/:id:int   {"title"?: "...", "done"?: bool}
    DELETE /todos/:id:int   204 or 404

  What a route takes and gives is said once, as a shape. A handler reads what
  it was sent through a binder, which goes by its route's shape, checks each
  field and lists everything that is wrong in one 400. It answers with a
  response or raises: the binder's error, an error that carries a problem of
  its own, and whatever the store raised for what the store refused.
